<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cocijoeza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th–16th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cocijoeza was the Zapotec king of Zaachila in the late 15th and early 16th centuries. Around 1490 he conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isthmus-of-tehuantepec">Isthmus of Tehuantepec</a> and moved his seat there, then resisted the Aztec ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahuitzotl">Ahuitzotl</a> in a long siege of the mountain fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guiengola">Guiengola</a>. Peace was sealed by his marriage to an Aztec princess, and their son Cocijopii ruled Tehuantepec when the Spanish arrived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cocijoeza.jpg" alt="Cocijoeza" width="309" height="631" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Rivera · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reyzapoteca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
